jon snow house of the dragon the sea  snake let's review every game of thrones  spin-off currently in development as  well as every rumored series still on  the horizon  there are currently seven game of  thrones spin-offs in development that we  know about while the final season of  game of thrones may have left a sour  taste in many viewers mouths the  excitement for shows like house of the  dragon and the now confirmed jon snow  sequel series is at an all-time high  today we're going to be breaking down  everything we know about the 7 spin-offs  in development and stick around to the  end to find out how one spin-off was  quickly cancelled costing hbo over 30  million dollars  [Music]  the first game of thrones spin-off on  our list and the one i'm most excited  about is the untitled jon snow sequel  series with the working title snow kit  harrington is set to reprise his role as  jon snow after his exile in game of  thrones when he went to live with the  wildlings north of the wall along with  his friend tormund giant spain it's  still uncertain whether the show will  follow jon and his adventures north of  the wall or if he'll be pulled back into  the politics of the south seeing as how  he's now living with the wildlings we  may even get to see flashbacks to jon's  time with his first love interest egret  played by kitt harrington's real-life  wife rose leslie since jon snow's story  was one of the most exciting out of any  character from game of thrones this show  is sure to be one of the most highly  anticipated spin-offs in this list we  still don't know much about the show or  whether it will ever make it out of the  development stage but we can be sure  that its potential for success certainly  depends on the success of the next  spin-off in our list house of the dragon  based on george rr martin's book fire  and blood house of the dragon picks up  the story 200 years before game of  thrones the first season of the show is  currently being released and a second  season has already been confirmed the  show follows the war of succession  within the house targaryen called the  dance of dragons house of the dragon  will have 10 episodes in the first  season and it's been so popular that  when the pilot was released it actually  caused hbo max's servers to crash it'll  be exciting to see where this series  takes us and how it may cross over with  the next spin-off on our list the sea  snake one of the most striking  characters from the house of the dragon  was the master of ships on the king's  council lord corliss velaryon played by  steve tucson also known as the sea snake  corliss earned his reputation through  his infamous adventures as a naval  warrior which this series is likely to  follow the sea snake is currently being  written by the mentalist creator bruno  heller prior to pitching the sea snake  heller also approached hbo about a  prequel series focused on robert  baratheon and ned stark's rebellion  against the mad king which immediately  precedes game of thrones so there could  be one more spin-off in the works  somewhere surrounding the story of  robert's rebellion quick plug if you  like what you're seeing hit that  subscribe button to see more videos like  this now on to the next series in our  list another spin-off in development  following some adventurers in westerosi  waters is titled ten thousand ships set  a thousand years before game of thrones  the series is set to focus on a key  figure within westerosi legend princess  nymeria the founder of dorne nymeri was  mentioned both in house of the dragon  and game of thrones in which arya stark  chose the name nymeria for her direwolf  her journey will take her to many  different lands around the summer sea  from the dinosaur-infested jungles of  cethorios to the tropical paradise of  the summer islands before she finally  migrates to dorne where she'll set the  roots for the ancestors of the modern  dornishmen and house martel ten thousand  ships is one of the show's furthest  along in its development and the sea  snake's title was even changed from its  original name the nine voyages to avoid  too many titles with numbers in them  person of interest writer amanda segel  has been attached to 10 000 ships and  george rr martin has said that the  project is progressing quite well the  next spin-off series will feature the  iconic knight sir duncan the tall or  dunk and esquire egg who is destined to  become king aegon targaryen v this  series has a couple of rumored names  including dunkin egg and a knight of the  seven kingdoms the series will likely  have three seasons closely adapting the  stories from george rr martin's novellas  the hedge knight the sworn sword and the  mystery knight all of which take place  approximately 90 years before game of  thrones helmed by steve conrad this  series is expected to be a very faithful  adaptation of martin's stories which is  exactly what martin wants according to  his personal blog the next series in our  list is actually an animated series with  the working title the golden empire and  it's set to take place in yiti a country  in essos loosely based on imperial china  martin has only said that a young writer  is working on the show but that the  early artwork is stunning it's likely  the story will follow the collapse of  the great empire of the dawn and it may  surround the civil war between the  transition of power between two great  dynasties early on in the history of ut  next up on our list of spin-offs is a  prequel to game of thrones set and flea  bottom the slums of king's landing this  area is notorious for its high level of  crime and it's where the poorest  residents of the westeros capital live  it's in these areas where characters  such as sir davos seaworth and gendry  baratheon were raised and it's likely  that if this series makes it out of  development that the story will follow  one of these characters or another we've  seen before in game of thrones now that  we know every game of thrones spin-off  currently in development let's talk  about how hbo mistakenly lost over 30  million dollars on one episode of a  spin-off that's never seen the light of  day  the series was titled blood moon and it  took place during the long night around  8 000 years before the time of game of  thrones this wasn't an easy project to  develop especially since martin had only  written a few sentences about the time  period across all of his books martin  himself admitted blood moon was a very  difficult assignment we're dealing with  a much more primitive people there were  no dragons yet however showrunner jane  goldman pushed on to create a 30 million  dollar pilot episode one of the most  expensive pilots ever made the episode  featured naomi watts as well as several  other talented cast members and it  surrounded a wedding between a great  northern house and a southern house but  hbl pulled the plug on the project in  late 2019. robert greenblatt the former  chairman of hbo's parent company warner  media said about the show it wasn't  unwatchable or horrible or anything it  was very well produced and looked  extraordinary but it didn't take me to  the same place as the original series it  didn't have that depth and richness that  the original series pilot did the  strangest thing about it all though  george rr martin still hasn't seen the  pilot episode it was locked away likely  alongside the original unaired pilot for  game of thrones which was almost  entirely re-shot and recast if martin  hasn't seen blood moon's pilot and hbo  execs weren't willing to do reshoots for  the episode i think it's pretty likely  the show was well beyond saving but what  do you think about this 30 million  dollar blunder drop your thoughts in the  comment section below also check out the  video on your screen for some more of my  content don't forget to like and  subscribe and thanks for watching rocket  riley
 

